.SH NAME
anpu-completion-bash - Generate the autocompletion script for bash


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu completion bash\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for the bash shell.

.PP
This script depends on the 'bash-completion' package.
If it is not installed already, you can install it via your OS's package manager.

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(anpu completion bash)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
anpu completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/anpu
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
anpu completion bash > $(brew --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/anpu
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for bash

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu-completion(1)\fP


